n, southwestern, and midwestern areas of the United States. The company offers fashion apparel for men, women, and children; accessories, cosmetics, home furnishings, and other consumer goods through dillards.com, an Internet store and clearance centers. It also engages in the general contracting construction activities, such as constructing and remodeling stores for the company. The company was founded in 1938 and is based in Little Rock, Arkansas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William T. Dillard II | Chairman & CEO | Age 80 | Compensation: $4.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10). Recent headlines include layoff or workforce-reduction announcements.","financial_summary":["Dillard's, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $9.7B market cap on $6.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years and -0% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 80% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 70-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 35%.","The business throws off $624M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.26\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 17\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 6.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 32% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (28.6% of 